To determine the probability that a student likes neither blue nor green, we can use the principle of inclusion-exclusion. 

The probability of liking blue is 58%, the probability of liking green is 45%, and the probability of liking both is 22%. 

Using the formula:
P(neither) = 100% - P(blue) - P(green) + P(both)
P(neither) = 100% - 58% - 45% + 22% = 15%.

Therefore, the probability that a student likes neither color is 15%.

